    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d126">

                <pb facs="0146" n="132" sameAs="frus:frus1943v06/pg132"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.51/1100: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Des Portes</hi>)<anchor
                        n="59" xml:id="d126-f1"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-07-15T19:00:00-06:00">July 15, 1943—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:59 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>537. Reference my telegram No. 536, July 15, 11 a.m.,<anchor n="58"
                        xml:id="d126-f2"/> and Department’s airgram No. 396, April 3. The President
                    has just informed me that the Supreme Court decision was favorable to the fruit
                    company by a vote of 4 to 1 and that the decision will be made public early next
                    week.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Des Portes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d126-f1" n="59" type="source" xml:id="d126-f1-content">
                <p>The Legation in Costa Rica was elevated to the status of Embassy on May 20, 1943,
                    when Ambassador Fay Allen Des Portes, succeeding Minister Robert M. Scotten,
                    presented his credentials to the Costa Rican Government.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d126-f2" n="58" xml:id="d126-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
